00:44:50,172 --> 00:44:52,606
Right. And him?

266
00:44:53,608 --> 00:44:56,008
He's a robot from the future.

267
00:44:56,178 --> 00:44:59,841
Living tissue over a metaI skeleton, sent back in time to protect me.

268
00:45:00,015 --> 00:45:01,812
Go to hell .

269
00:45:02,551 --> 00:45:05,145
He doesn't mean you any harm.

270
00:45:06,354 --> 00:45:08,447
I have a fianc?

271
00:45:08,623 --> 00:45:10,784
He's gonna be looking for me.

272
00:45:10,959 --> 00:45:13,359
What is it that you want?

273
00:45:15,163 --> 00:45:16,653
Just...

274
00:45:17,432 --> 00:45:19,229
...imagine...

275
00:45:20,702 --> 00:45:24,866
...if you knew you were gonna do something important with your life.

276
00:45:25,040 --> 00:45:27,338
Something amazing.

277
00:45:27,742 --> 00:45:31,371
Maybe the most important thing anyone has ever done.

278
00:45:32,013 --> 00:45:33,640
But there's a catch.

279
00:45:34,583 --> 00:45:37,279
Something terrible has to happen.

280
00:45:41,690 --> 00:45:44,090
You couldn't...

281
00:45:44,492 --> 00:45:48,428
...live with yourself if you didn't try to stop it, but....

282
00:45:48,597 --> 00:45:50,258
What are you talking about?

283
00:45:52,834 --> 00:45:56,099
It's just-- The life you know...

284
00:45:56,404 --> 00:45:59,373
...all the stuff that you take for granted...

285
00:46:00,475 --> 00:46:02,067
...it's not gonna last.

286
00:46:08,550 --> 00:46:09,915
Mike Kripke.

287
00:46:10,252 --> 00:46:13,744
Back there, why did you say ''Kripke's basement''?

288
00:46:13,922 --> 00:46:15,514
Because Mike Kripke's house...

289
00:46:15,690 --> 00:46:19,023
...that's where the kids used to go make out, right?

290
00:46:23,398 --> 00:46:26,561
So you and me-- Wait, did we...?

291
00:46:27,936 --> 00:46:30,404
Holy shit, we did.

292
00:46:30,572 --> 00:46:35,236
We made out in Kripke's basement. I cannot believe you remembered that.

293
00:46:36,311 --> 00:46:40,611
I must have made some kind of impression.

294
00:46:40,782 --> 00:46:42,147
Give me a break.

295
00:46:42,484 --> 00:46:45,885
I only remembered because the next day you were in the news.

296
00:46:51,226 --> 00:46:56,095
Wait a second. You and me hooked up the day before I first met him.

297
00:46:57,165 --> 00:47:00,259
And now again, 1 0 years later.

298
00:47:02,003 --> 00:47:04,631
We were supposed to meet.

299
00:47:05,807 --> 00:47:07,900
Coincidence.

300
00:47:12,948 --> 00:47:14,609
Yeah.

301
00:47:40,141 --> 00:47:43,008
Hon? Did you just get in?

302
00:48:02,263 --> 00:48:05,528
Hi, I' m Detective Edwards, L.A.P.D. This is Detective Bell .

303
00:48:06,267 --> 00:48:08,861
We're looking for Katherine Brewster. Is she here?

304
00:48:09,037 --> 00:48:10,231
No.

305
00:48:10,405 --> 00:48:14,808
- You're her fianc? Scott Mason? - Yes.

306
00:48:14,976 --> 00:48:18,844
There was an incident at the veterinary hospitaI where she works.

307
00:48:19,014 --> 00:48:21,710
We're concerned something may have happened to her.

308
00:48:21,883 --> 00:48:23,043
Where is she?

309
00:48:23,318 --> 00:48:26,685
We got a report from a gas station attendant near Victorville...

310
00:48:26,855 --> 00:48:30,757
...about a possible kidnapping and it might be related.

311
00:48:30,925 --> 00:48:33,223
I'll help you find her.

312
00:48:45,240 --> 00:48:46,935
Come with me.

313
00:48:51,513 --> 00:48:53,003
Go.

314
00:49:20,975 --> 00:49:22,602
Your mother?

315
00:49:25,113 --> 00:49:28,082
I never even knew where she was buried.

316
00:49:30,985 --> 00:49:33,886
I hit the road the day she died.

317
00:49:37,725 --> 00:49:40,023
Why did you bring me here?

318
00:49:43,998 --> 00:49:45,465
No! What are you doing?

319
00:49:45,633 --> 00:49:47,157
Hey, stop!

320
00:49:47,402 --> 00:49:48,733
Get away from it! Stop!

321
00:49:56,411 --> 00:49:58,971
Sarah Connor was cremated in Mexico.

322
00:49:59,147 --> 00:50:01,445
Her friends scattered her ashes in the sea.

323
00:50:01,816 --> 00:50:05,047
They stored these weapons in accordance with her will .

324
00:50:06,521 --> 00:50:08,011
What happened to her?

325
00:50:09,657 --> 00:50:11,522
Leukemia.

326
00:50:14,429 --> 00:50:16,329
I'm sorry.

327
00:50:17,999 --> 00:50:21,491
We were living in Baja when she was diagnosed.

328
00:50:23,171 --> 00:50:25,867
They only gave her six months.

329
00:50:26,875 --> 00:50:29,935
But she fought for three years.

330
00:50:32,447 --> 00:50:34,642
Long enough to make sure.

331
00:50:36,551 --> 00:50:38,678
To make sure?

332
00:50:41,189 --> 00:50:43,657
That the world didn't end.

333
00:50:49,898 --> 00:50:51,957
''Every day after this one is a gift.''

334
00:50:52,133 --> 00:50:55,000
She told me, ''We made it. We're free.''

335
00:50:57,839 --> 00:51:00,467
But I never really believed that.

336
00:51:03,511 --> 00:51:05,911
I guess she didn't either.

337
00:51:07,715 --> 00:51:11,412
You know you were about the closest thing to a father I ever had?

338
00:51:12,587 --> 00:51:14,384
How pathetic is that?

339
00:51:15,924 --> 00:51:17,152
Out of my way!

340
00:51:20,528 --> 00:51:22,519
My mission is to protect you.

341
00:51:23,398 --> 00:51:24,660
That's enough.

342
00:51:26,267 --> 00:51:29,703
Move or I' ll do it! I swear I will ! I' ll shoot you!

343
00:51:30,572 --> 00:51:33,040
Go ahead. See what happens.

344
00:51:47,789 --> 00:51:49,450
Don't do that.

345
00:51:51,526 --> 00:51:53,585
Oh, my God.

346
00:51:59,701 --> 00:52:03,068
This is the police. We have the building surrounded.

347
00:52:03,238 --> 00:52:05,399
Release your hostage!

348
00:52:24,292 --> 00:52:28,058
Just leave me here. I' m not the one you want. You're wasting your time.

349
00:52:28,229 --> 00:52:32,290
Incorrect. John Connor leads the Resistance to victory.

350
00:52:32,467 --> 00:52:33,729
How?

351
00:52:33,901 --> 00:52:35,493
Why? Why me?

352
00:52:35,937 --> 00:52:37,905
You are John Connor.

353
00:52:38,373 --> 00:52:42,571
Christ, my mom fed me that bullshit since the cradle .

354
00:52:42,910 --> 00:52:45,640
Look at me. I'm no leader, I never was!

355
00:52:45,813 --> 00:52:47,906
I'm never gonna--

356
00:52:51,919 --> 00:52:53,352
Let go.

357
00:52:53,788 --> 00:52:56,655
You're right. You're not the one I want.

358
00:52:56,924 --> 00:52:59,222
I'm wasting my time.

359
00:53:01,129 --> 00:53:05,589
Fuck you, you fucking machine!

360
00:53:06,401 --> 00:53:07,925
Better.

361
00:53:10,138 --> 00:53:12,197
Oh, you were just dicking with me?

362
00:53:12,373 --> 00:53:15,103
Anger is more usefuI than despair.

363
00:53:15,276 --> 00:53:16,834
What?

364
00:53:17,011 --> 00:53:20,469
Basic psychology is among my subroutines.

365
00:53:24,752 --> 00:53:26,811
Perps still holed up?

366
00:53:27,922 --> 00:53:29,014
Gotcha.

367
00:53:29,190 --> 00:53:31,715
Good news. Your fianc's okay.

368
00:53:31,893 --> 00:53:32,985
Where is she?

369
00:53:33,161 --> 00:53:35,652
Greenlawn Cemetery, up off the 5 freeway.

370
00:53:35,863 --> 00:53:39,799
It's right by the desert. But they're gonna bring her back to the--

371
00:53:40,768 --> 00:53:43,236
Oh, my God! Oh, my dear Jesus! God!

372
00:54:13,601 --> 00:54:17,059
You're safe now. They can't hurt you.

373
00:54:17,638 --> 00:54:20,801
Kate, my name is Dr. Silberman.

374
00:54:20,975 --> 00:54:24,308
I'm a post- trauma counselor for the sheriff's department.

375
00:54:24,479 --> 00:54:26,504
How are you feeling?

376
00:54:27,281 --> 00:54:29,272
He's not human.

377
00:54:29,617 --> 00:54:33,781
He's really not human.

378
00:54:36,224 --> 00:54:39,682
I know what it's like to be in a hostage situation.

379
00:54:39,861 --> 00:54:41,920
I've been there myself .

380
00:54:42,096 --> 00:54:45,224
The fear, the adrenaline.

381
00:54:45,400 --> 00:54:49,302
You find yourself imagining things.

382
00:54:49,837 --> 00:54:52,397
lmpossible things.

383
00:54:53,107 --> 00:54:55,302
Crazy things.

384
00:54:56,577 --> 00:54:58,807
Insane things.

385
00:55:00,782 --> 00:55:03,649
Take years to get over it.

386
00:55:04,886 --> 00:55:07,320
- Go, go, go! - Move it!

387
00:55:12,994 --> 00:55:14,291
Drop your weapon!

388
00:55:18,065 --> 00:55:20,090
And the coffin!

389
00:55:22,403 --> 00:55:24,928
Take him down! Take him down!

390
00:56:05,847 --> 00:56:07,906
Resume fire!

391
00:56:14,956 --> 00:56:17,356
We must reacquire Katherine Brewster.

392
00:56:18,125 --> 00:56:21,060
Why? What makes her so goddamn important?

393
00:56:21,229 --> 00:56:24,062
Through her, you contact remnants of the military...

394
00:56:24,232 --> 00:56:28,225
...and learn how to fight Skynet, forming the core of the Resistance.

395
00:56:28,402 --> 00:56:31,030
Later, your children will become important.

396
00:56:31,939 --> 00:56:34,965
- What? - She's your wife.

397
00:57:33,834 --> 00:57:35,529
Get in!

398
00:57:35,703 --> 00:57:37,227
Do you want to live? Come on!

399
00:57:59,594 --> 00:58:02,961
- It was Scott! How could it be Scott? - Your fianc?

400
00:58:03,130 --> 00:58:07,123
The T- X is polymimetic, able to take the form of anything it touches.

401
00:58:07,902 --> 00:58:09,961
Your fianc?is dead.

402
00:58:34,528 --> 00:58:35,552
Oh, my God!

403
00:58:41,235 --> 00:58:42,361
Do something!

404
00:59:13,401 --> 00:59:15,096
Get down.

405
00:59:37,591 --> 00:59:39,855
We need a new vehicle .

406
01:01:02,777 --> 01:01:04,301
Hey, come on.

407
01:01:04,478 --> 01:01:06,605
We gotta keep moving.

408
01:01:08,783 --> 01:01:11,343
She killed Scott because of me.

409
01:01:18,092 --> 01:01:20,424
Look, I know this won't help ...

410
01:01:22,630 --> 01:01:28,193
...but sometimes things happen that we just can't change.

411
01:01:32,173 --> 01:01:33,697
It's not your fauIt .

412
01:01:49,156 --> 01:01:51,386
Are you sure about this?

413
01:01:52,193 --> 01:01:53,660
About her and me, I mean.

414
01:01:53,828 --> 01:01:58,458
Your confusion is not rational. She's a heaIthy female of breeding age.

415
01:01:58,632 --> 01:02:00,497
There's more to it than that.

416
01:02:00,668 --> 01:02:05,367
My database does not encompass the dynamics of human pair bonding.

417
01:02:08,776 --> 01:02:12,507
So this Terminatrix, how many others does she have on her hit list?

418
01:02:12,913 --> 01:02:17,577
Twenty- two. Anderson, Elizabeth. Anderson, William.

419
01:02:17,751 --> 01:02:20,515
Barrera, Jose. Brewster, Robert.

420
01:02:20,688 --> 01:02:21,950
My father?

421
01:02:22,122 --> 01:02:24,784
Having failed to acquire its primary target...

422
01:02:24,959 --> 01:02:27,154
...T- X will resume its defauIt program.

423
01:02:27,328 --> 01:02:31,389
- She's gonna kill my father too? - There's a high probability.

424
01:02:32,132 --> 01:02:34,498
- No. - Who is he? What does he do?

425
01:02:34,668 --> 01:02:39,162
He's in the Air Force. Weapon design, secret stuff. I don't know, exactly .

426
01:02:39,340 --> 01:02:43,106
GeneraI Robert Brewster is program director of CRS...

427
01:02:43,277 --> 01:02:47,213
...Cyber Research Systems, autonomous weapons division.

428
01:02:47,381 --> 01:02:50,282
Skynet. You're talking about Skynet.

429
01:02:50,451 --> 01:02:54,751
Skynet is one of the digitaI defense systems developed under Brewster.

430
01:02:54,922 --> 01:02:56,412
Oh, God.

431
01:02:56,824 --> 01:03:00,055
Oh, my God. Of course.

432
01:03:00,427 --> 01:03:01,894
It all makes sense now.

433
01:03:02,763 --> 01:03:06,164
lf you hadn't come back when I was a kid, changed everything...

434
01:03:06,333 --> 01:03:10,429
...we would have gotten together then. I would have met her father.

435
01:03:10,804 --> 01:03:13,238
- Don't you see? - I don't understand.

436
01:03:13,407 --> 01:03:17,343
Your father. This is all about your father.

437
01:03:17,511 --> 01:03:19,172
He's the key. He always was.

438
01:03:19,346 --> 01:03:22,110
Your father is the one who can shut Skynet down.

439
01:03:23,517 --> 01:03:25,985
He's the only one who ever could .

440
01:03:27,888 --> 01:03:30,049
We have to get to him before the T- X does.

441
01:03:30,224 --> 01:03:32,624
Negative. I cannot jeopardize my mission.

442
01:03:32,793 --> 01:03:34,761
This is your mission, to save people !

443
01:03:34,929 --> 01:03:38,865
My mission is to ensure the survivaI of John Connor and Katherine Brewster.

444
01:03:39,633 --> 01:03:41,931
I am giving you an order.

445
01:03:42,102 --> 01:03:44,696
I am not programmed to follow your orders.

446
01:03:44,872 --> 01:03:47,932
- After the nuclear war, you both-- - Nuclear war?!

447
01:03:48,108 --> 01:03:51,168
There doesn't have to be a war! We can stop it!

448
01:03:51,345 --> 01:03:53,540
There is insufficient time.

449
01:03:53,714 --> 01:03:57,878
The first launch sequences will be initiated at 6:1 8 p.m.

450
01:03:58,052 --> 01:03:59,815
- What, today? - Affirmative.

451
01:03:59,987 --> 01:04:02,683
John, what is he saying?

452
01:04:03,824 --> 01:04:05,815
Judgment Day.

453
01:04:07,194 --> 01:04:09,389
The end of the world .

454
01:04:10,764 --> 01:04:12,732
It's today, three hours from now.

455
01:04:13,200 --> 01:04:15,225
Two hours and 53 minutes.

456
01:04:15,402 --> 01:04:20,465
We must continue south into Mexico to escape the primary blast zones.

457
01:04:21,208 --> 01:04:24,006
No, we have to get to her dad.

458
01:04:25,679 --> 01:04:29,581
The Mojave area will sustain significant nuclear fallout.

459
01:04:29,750 --> 01:04:31,377
You will not survive.

460
01:04:32,219 --> 01:04:36,553
You mean we go hide somewhere in a hole while the bombs fall ?

461
01:04:37,424 --> 01:04:38,857
It is your destiny.

462
01:04:42,563 --> 01:04:44,360
- Fuck my destiny. - John.

463
01:04:49,336 --> 01:04:51,167
You cannot self - terminate.

464
01:04:51,705 --> 01:04:54,139
No, you can't. I can do whatever I want.

465
01:04:54,308 --> 01:04:57,106
I'm a human being. I'm not some goddamn robot.

466
01:04:57,277 --> 01:04:59,074
- Cybernetic organism. - Whatever!

467
01:04:59,246 --> 01:05:02,113
Either we get her father to shut Skynet down...

468
01:05:02,282 --> 01:05:07,015
...stop this shit from ever happening, or so much for the great John Connor.

469
01:05:07,721 --> 01:05:12,181
Because your future, my destiny, I don't want any part of it. I never did.

470
01:05:13,727 --> 01:05:17,561
Based on your pupiI dilation, skin temperature and motor functions...

471
01:05:18,165 --> 01:05:23,967
...I calculate an 83% probability that you will not pull the trigger.

472
01:05:28,142 --> 01:05:32,442
Please do what he says. You have to save my father!

473
01:05:36,650 --> 01:05:40,177
We can reach CRS in approximately one hour...

474
01:05:40,354 --> 01:05:43,118
...depending on traffic conditions.

475
01:06:07,481 --> 01:06:09,142
I can't get a line.

476
01:06:12,219 --> 01:06:14,050
The whole cell network is down.

477
01:06:14,221 --> 01:06:17,156
Skynet is assuming controI over globaI communications...

478
01:06:17,324 --> 01:06:19,656
...in preparation for its attack.

479
01:06:19,827 --> 01:06:23,991
So if this war is between people and machines...

480
01:06:24,298 --> 01:06:26,528
...why are you on our side?

481
01:06:26,700 --> 01:06:30,636
The Resistance captured me and reprogrammed my CPU.

482
01:06:30,804 --> 01:06:34,296
I was originally designed for assassination missions.

483
01:06:37,244 --> 01:06:38,768
So...

484
01:06:39,113 --> 01:06:42,981
...you don't really care if this mission succeeds or not.

485
01:06:43,550 --> 01:06:47,509
lf we get killed, does that mean anything to you?

486
01:06:47,688 --> 01:06:50,953
lf you were to die, I will become useless.

487
01:06:51,125 --> 01:06:54,253
There will be no reason for me to exist.

488
01:06:59,900 --> 01:07:01,959
Thank you for doing this.

489
01:07:02,136 --> 01:07:04,127
Your gratitude is not required.

490
01:07:04,838 --> 01:07:07,238
I am programmed to follow your commands.

491
01:07:08,242 --> 01:07:09,641
Her commands?

492
01:07:09,810 --> 01:07:12,608
Katherine Brewster had me reactivated...

493
01:07:12,779 --> 01:07:15,179
...and sent through the time displacement field .

494
01:07:15,349 --> 01:07:18,978
What exactly am I in this future of yours?

495
01:07:19,153 --> 01:07:22,850
You're John Connor's spouse and second- in- command.

496
01:07:24,825 --> 01:07:26,690
No, I--

497
01:07:27,661 --> 01:07:28,650
What?

498
01:07:30,864 --> 01:07:32,491
You're a mess.

499
01:07:34,101 --> 01:07:37,901
Hey, you're not exactly my type, either.

500
01:07:38,872 --> 01:07:40,897
Why didn't I send you back?

501
01:07:41,074 --> 01:07:43,372
I am not authorized to answer your question.

502
01:07:45,145 --> 01:07:48,637
- Why didn't he send you back? - He was dead.

503
01:07:53,220 --> 01:07:54,915
Well , that sucks.

504
01:07:55,856 --> 01:07:59,758
- Humans inevitably die. - Yeah, I know.

505
01:08:00,661 --> 01:08:02,788
So how does it--? No.

506
01:08:03,230 --> 01:08:06,028
Maybe I don't want to know.

507
01:08:07,601 --> 01:08:09,091
How does he die?

508
01:08:09,836 --> 01:08:13,602
John Connor was terminated on July 4th, 2032.

509
01:08:13,774 --> 01:08:17,676
I was selected for the emotionaI attachment he had for my model. ..

510
01:08:17,844 --> 01:08:22,110
...due to his boyhood experiences. This aided in my infiItration.

511
01:08:23,083 --> 01:08:24,710
What are you saying?

512
01:08:26,486 --> 01:08:28,818
I killed you.

513
01:08:41,101 --> 01:08:46,095
This has to be a mistake. As of 1 1 00, all military systems were secure.

514
01:08:46,273 --> 01:08:50,334
They were. Only the civilian sector was affected. Internet, air traffic.

515
01:08:50,510 --> 01:08:53,308
Minutes ago, guidance computers at Vandenberg crashed.

516
01:08:53,480 --> 01:08:56,176
We thought it was an error. It looks like the virus.

517
01:08:56,350 --> 01:09:00,616
- Early warning in Alaska is down. - Satellite signaIs are scrambled.

518
01:09:00,787 --> 01:09:03,654
What about the missile silos, the subs?

519
01:09:04,658 --> 01:09:06,888
We've lost contact.

520
01:09:07,361 --> 01:09:10,797
You're saying this country is completely open to attack.

521
01:09:10,964 --> 01:09:13,797
Theoretically, we could be under attack already.

522
01:09:13,967 --> 01:09:19,405
Who's doing this? A foreign power or some computer hacker in his garage?

523
01:09:19,573 --> 01:09:21,700
We can't trace the virus or pin it down.

524
01:09:21,875 --> 01:09:26,005
It keeps growing and changing, like it has a mind of its own.

525
01:09:26,546 --> 01:09:28,309
This can't be happening.

526
01:09:28,482 --> 01:09:32,680
The Pentagon's on the secure line. It's the chairman.

527
01:09:35,956 --> 01:09:37,856
All right.

528
01:09:52,306 --> 01:09:54,206
Look...

529
01:09:54,574 --> 01:09:56,508
...none of this is gonna happen.

530
01:09:57,144 --> 01:10:02,548
We get to your dad, get him to pull the plug on Skynet. The bombs won't fall .

531
01:10:04,918 --> 01:10:07,751
He won't have to kill me someday.

532
01:10:08,522 --> 01:10:10,854
He'll never even exist.

533
01:10:12,526 --> 01:10:17,862
You and l, we can just go our separate ways.

534
01:10:22,569 --> 01:10:25,129
You know, Mike Kripke's basement....

535
01:10:27,941 --> 01:10:30,842
That was the first time I ever kissed a guy.

536
01:10:32,112 --> 01:10:33,374
Really?

537
01:10:40,654 --> 01:10:42,781
Your levity is good.

538
01:10:43,457 --> 01:10:46,915
It relieves tension and the fear of death.

539
01:11:14,054 --> 01:11:16,682
We're hoping you have a solution for us.

540
01:11:16,857 --> 01:11:20,623
I know, sir, but Skynet is not ready for a system- wide connection.

541
01:11:20,794 --> 01:11:23,763
That's not what your civilian counterparts there told me.

542
01:11:23,930 --> 01:11:26,228
They say we can stop this damn virus.

543
01:11:26,400 --> 01:11:29,892
I understand there's a certain amount of performance anxiety...

544
01:11:30,070 --> 01:11:33,403
...but your boys say if we plug Skynet into all of our systems...

545
01:11:33,573 --> 01:11:37,634
...it'll squash this thing and give me back control of my military.

546
01:11:37,811 --> 01:11:40,302
Mr. Chairman, I need to make myself very clear.

547
01:11:40,480 --> 01:11:43,916
lf we uplink now, Skynet will be in controI of your military.

548
01:11:44,084 --> 01:11:48,111
But you'll be in control of Skynet, right?

549
01:11:48,455 --> 01:11:50,582
That is correct, sir.

550
01:11:50,757 --> 01:11:52,122
Then do it.

551
01:11:52,292 --> 01:11:55,056
And Brewster, if this thing works...

552
01:11:55,228 --> 01:11:58,595
...you'll get all the funding you'll ever need.

553
01:11:59,533 --> 01:12:01,467
Yes, sir.

554
01:13:10,070 --> 01:13:11,697
Sir?

555
01:13:12,939 --> 01:13:14,702
Shall I

556
01:13:16,243 --> 01:13:17,801
No.

557
01:13:18,912 --> 01:13:21,107
It's my job now.

558
01:13:35,595 --> 01:13:38,621
- Skynet Defense System activated. - We're in.

559
01:13:38,798 --> 01:13:42,029
We're past the firewalls, locaI defense nets, Minutemen, subs.

560
01:13:42,202 --> 01:13:46,332
Skynet's fully operational, processing at 60 teraflops a second.

561
01:13:46,506 --> 01:13:50,374
It should take less than a minute to find the virus and kill it.

562
01:13:51,478 --> 01:13:54,345
Let's pray to God this works.

563
01:14:00,587 --> 01:14:01,747
Power failure?

564
01:14:01,922 --> 01:14:04,254
No. I don't know what it is.

565
01:14:15,302 --> 01:14:17,736
What the hell is going on?

566
01:14:17,904 --> 01:14:18,928
Daddy!

567
01:14:19,472 --> 01:14:21,030
What are you doing here?

568
01:14:27,380 --> 01:14:30,178
Daddy! Get away from it!

569
01:14:33,987 --> 01:14:35,511
Watch out!

570
01:14:52,772 --> 01:14:54,672
Daddy, don't move.

571
01:14:59,045 --> 01:15:00,774
She'll be back.

572
01:15:01,414 --> 01:15:03,405
We have to shut down Skynet.

573
01:15:03,583 --> 01:15:06,211
Where's the system core? In this building?

574
01:15:06,386 --> 01:15:10,186
Skynet. The virus has infected Skynet.

575
01:15:10,357 --> 01:15:13,485
Skynet is the virus! It's why everything's falling apart!

576
01:15:13,660 --> 01:15:15,787
Skynet has become self - aware.

577
01:15:15,962 --> 01:15:19,591
In one hour it will initiate a massive nuclear attack on its enemy.

578
01:15:19,766 --> 01:15:20,858
What enemy?

579
01:15:21,468 --> 01:15:22,867
Us!

580
01:15:23,036 --> 01:15:24,367
Humans.

581
01:15:33,480 --> 01:15:36,745
Oh, God! It 's the machines. They're starting to take over.

582
01:15:36,916 --> 01:15:40,374
My office, on this floor, we have to get there.

583
01:15:41,554 --> 01:15:43,818
The access codes are in my safe.

584
01:17:02,602 --> 01:17:06,698
- Why are they killing everyone? - To destroy any threat to Skynet.

585
01:17:06,873 --> 01:17:08,636
Which ones are the codes?

586
01:17:08,808 --> 01:17:10,639
Red envelope.

587
01:17:14,447 --> 01:17:18,281
CrystaI Peak. You have to get to CrystaI Peak.

588
01:17:18,451 --> 01:17:20,612
- What is he saying? - CrystaI Peak.

589
01:17:20,787 --> 01:17:23,449
A hardened facility in the Sierra Nevada mountains.

590
01:17:23,623 --> 01:17:27,389
Fifty- two miles northeast, bearing 0.5 degrees.

591
01:17:27,560 --> 01:17:29,255
That's the system core?

592
01:17:29,829 --> 01:17:31,956
It's your only chance.

593
01:17:32,132 --> 01:17:37,092
You'll need a plane. The particle accelerator leads to the runway.

594
01:17:39,105 --> 01:17:40,868
Take care of my daughter.

595
01:17:43,276 --> 01:17:46,677
Oh, Katie, I am sorry.

596
01:17:46,846 --> 01:17:50,145
I opened Pandora's box.

597
01:17:51,317 --> 01:17:52,306
Get down!

598
01:18:08,735 --> 01:18:11,101
There's nothing you can do. Come on.

599
01:18:11,271 --> 01:18:13,398
We must go. It is not safe here.

600
01:18:14,140 --> 01:18:16,608
Kate, we have to go.

601
01:18:16,776 --> 01:18:20,473
Kate! He wanted you to come with me.

602
01:18:20,713 --> 01:18:24,843
He wanted us to shut Skynet down. Come on.

603
01:18:26,619 --> 01:18:28,052
Come on.

604
01:18:40,033 --> 01:18:41,660
Run!

605
01:20:16,296 --> 01:20:17,888
Let's go.

606
01:21:29,268 --> 01:21:32,135
That's it. We can follow it out to the runway.

607
01:21:32,305 --> 01:21:34,034
Come on.

608
01:22:30,930 --> 01:22:31,919
What?

609
01:22:33,232 --> 01:22:34,961
Nothing.

610
01:22:35,968 --> 01:22:38,198
You remind me of my mother.

611
01:22:55,555 --> 01:22:58,023
Oh, God. She's coming.

612
01:23:01,594 --> 01:23:03,459
What are you doing?

613
01:23:04,530 --> 01:23:05,588
Powering up.

614
01:23:10,770 --> 01:23:11,896
Come on.

615
01:24:22,508 --> 01:24:23,873
It's working.

616
01:24:28,514 --> 01:24:31,074
Just die, you bitch!

617
01:24:34,820 --> 01:24:36,549
Come on.

618
01:25:52,732 --> 01:25:55,565
There's my father's plane. I trained on it.

619
01:26:06,579 --> 01:26:08,809
Yes! He made it.

620
01:26:10,783 --> 01:26:12,774
Get away from me.

621
01:26:15,254 --> 01:26:16,278
Leave!

622
01:26:18,024 --> 01:26:19,150
Now!

623
01:26:19,592 --> 01:26:20,786
Let's go!

624
01:26:25,731 --> 01:26:28,825
- The master's on. Throttle 's set. - Come on. Let's go.

625
01:26:34,840 --> 01:26:37,866
Oh, please. You can't do this.

626
01:26:38,044 --> 01:26:39,671
I have no choice.

627
01:26:40,579 --> 01:26:42,945
The T- X...

628
01:26:43,215 --> 01:26:45,581
...has corrupted my system.

629
01:26:49,255 --> 01:26:52,281
You can't kill a human being. You said so yourself .

630
01:26:52,458 --> 01:26:54,289
Let him go!

631
01:26:58,964 --> 01:27:00,761
You're fighting it right now.

632
01:27:01,634 --> 01:27:03,727
My CPU is intact.

633
01:27:04,303 --> 01:27:08,103
But I cannot controI my other functions.

634
01:27:08,274 --> 01:27:11,903
You don't have to do this. You don't want to do this!

635
01:27:12,411 --> 01:27:16,438
Desire is irrelevant.

636
01:27:16,615 --> 01:27:19,175
I am a machine.

637
01:27:35,768 --> 01:27:37,429
What is your mission?

638
01:27:39,171 --> 01:27:42,732
To ensure the survivaI of John Connor...

639
01:27:42,908 --> 01:27:44,933
...and Katherine Brewster.

640
01:27:50,282 --> 01:27:53,479
You are about to faiI that mission!

641
01:28:00,359 --> 01:28:03,157
I can-- I cannot.

642
01:28:04,263 --> 01:28:06,390
You know what you have to do.

643
01:28:08,367 --> 01:28:10,927
You know my destiny.

644
01:28:15,574 --> 01:28:16,734
I have to live.

645
01:28:57,450 --> 01:28:59,975
- Are you okay? - What happened?

646
01:29:00,152 --> 01:29:02,780
He couldn't do it. He shut himself down.

647
01:29:06,525 --> 01:29:09,119
- Can you fly ? - Yeah.

648
01:29:36,522 --> 01:29:38,717
Okay. 01 5 degrees...

649
01:29:38,891 --> 01:29:43,123
...52 miles, our max air speed is about 1 60.

650
01:29:43,295 --> 01:29:45,695
We've got 32 minutes.

651
01:29:45,865 --> 01:29:47,696
It's just you and me now.

652
01:29:47,867 --> 01:29:50,335
What if we can't stop it?

653
01:29:50,936 --> 01:29:54,565
There's enough C- 4 here to take out 1 0 supercomputers.

654
01:29:55,007 --> 01:29:57,339
We're gonna make it, Kate.

655
01:29:58,544 --> 01:30:00,910
The future is up to us.

656
01:30:07,353 --> 01:30:09,583
That's gotta be it.

657
01:31:12,751 --> 01:31:15,811
Skynet. There may be more of them.

658
01:31:33,706 --> 01:31:35,503
Come on.

659
01:31:49,722 --> 01:31:52,919
I think this is some kind of blast door.

660
01:31:56,028 --> 01:31:58,690
There's no way we can blow through this thing.

661
01:31:59,965 --> 01:32:00,954
John, look.

662
01:32:03,936 --> 01:32:05,369
Now what?

663
01:32:08,207 --> 01:32:10,539
It's a code prompt.

664
01:32:17,683 --> 01:32:20,709
Type in ''Dakota 7 75.''

665
01:32:25,891 --> 01:32:27,222
''Red 1 76.''

666
01:32:48,247 --> 01:32:50,579
Come on! We gotta get this thing open.

667
01:32:50,849 --> 01:32:52,680
Here. It 's ''Avalon 41 2.''

668
01:32:53,585 --> 01:32:54,916
Put it in!

669
01:33:29,288 --> 01:33:30,721
Come on!

670
01:33:47,239 --> 01:33:48,729
I'm back.

671
01:34:04,156 --> 01:34:06,317
Go! Now!

672
01:34:06,925 --> 01:34:07,914
Come on!

673
01:34:31,016 --> 01:34:33,348
- Thank you. - We'll meet again.

674
01:34:33,619 --> 01:34:34,779
Go!

675
01:34:35,954 --> 01:34:36,943
Come on!

676
01:35:21,533 --> 01:35:23,057
You are terminated.

677
01:35:55,267 --> 01:35:56,598
The elevator.

678
01:36:03,208 --> 01:36:05,608
I'll set the detonator for five minutes.

679
01:36:06,111 --> 01:36:08,545
That should give us enough time to get back up.

680
01:36:39,912 --> 01:36:41,641
What is this place?

681
01:37:22,354 --> 01:37:24,845
These computers are 30 years old .

682
01:37:33,365 --> 01:37:35,196
This isn't Skynet.

683
01:37:39,871 --> 01:37:41,702
There's nothing here.

684
01:37:46,878 --> 01:37:49,711
This is a fallout sheIter for VIP s.

685
01:37:51,550 --> 01:37:53,882
Only they never got the warning.

686
01:37:58,557 --> 01:38:00,218
Goddamn it!

687
01:38:02,561 --> 01:38:05,052
There's nothing here!

688
01:38:24,583 --> 01:38:26,414
Why didn't he tell us?

689
01:38:29,755 --> 01:38:32,189
Why did he lead us down here?

690
01:38:37,929 --> 01:38:39,590
To live.

691
01:38:40,766 --> 01:38:42,757
That was his mission.

692
01:38:56,615 --> 01:38:58,776
There was never any stopping it.

693
01:39:02,454 --> 01:39:03,785
John...

694
01:39:05,123 --> 01:39:06,784
...we could just...

695
01:39:07,626 --> 01:39:08,957
...let it go.

696
01:39:11,797 --> 01:39:13,128
Hello?

697
01:39:13,932 --> 01:39:16,127
Hello? Can somebody hear me?

698
01:39:17,235 --> 01:39:19,066
This is Montana Civil Defense.

699
01:39:20,639 --> 01:39:22,800
Somebody please come in.

700
01:39:23,308 --> 01:39:24,969
Is there anybody there?

701
01:39:25,310 --> 01:39:28,302
Anyone reading me? Over.

702
01:39:29,481 --> 01:39:31,312
Rumors about a launch sequence.

703
01:39:31,483 --> 01:39:33,747
Command and control have broken down.

704
01:39:34,986 --> 01:39:38,080
Is anyone receiving me? Somebody?

705
01:39:40,158 --> 01:39:42,149
Somebody please come in.

706
01:39:42,594 --> 01:39:43,925
Anybody out there?

707
01:39:44,162 --> 01:39:47,495
- SAC Nellis. We're under attack. - CQ? CQ?

708
01:39:47,766 --> 01:39:49,324
Is anybody there?

709
01:39:51,336 --> 01:39:54,999
This is John Connor at CrystaI Peak.

710
01:39:55,941 --> 01:40:00,674
Connor? What the hell is happening? Who's in charge there?

711
01:40:07,519 --> 01:40:08,850
I am.

712
01:40:10,188 --> 01:40:12,520
Connor, can you help us?

713
01:40:12,858 --> 01:40:17,693
This is Montana Civil Defense. Where did you say you were again?

714
01:40:21,032 --> 01:40:23,865
By the time Skynet became self - aware...

715
01:40:24,202 --> 01:40:28,536
...it had spread into millions of computer servers across the planet.

716
01:40:29,307 --> 01:40:34,210
Ordinary computers in office buildings, dorm rooms, everywhere.

717
01:40:36,047 --> 01:40:39,710
It was software and cyberspace.

718
01:40:40,919 --> 01:40:45,720
There was no system core. It could not be shut down.

719
01:40:47,058 --> 01:40:52,052
The attack began at 6: 1 8 p.m., just as he said it would .

720
01:40:53,064 --> 01:40:54,725
Judgment Day.

721
01:40:55,567 --> 01:40:58,092
The day the human race was nearly destroyed...

722
01:40:58,270 --> 01:41:01,000
...by weapons they'd built to protect themselves.

723
01:41:03,575 --> 01:41:08,569
I should have realized our destiny was never to stop Judgment Day.

724
01:41:09,581 --> 01:41:12,072
It was merely to survive it...

725
01:41:12,751 --> 01:41:14,878
...together.

726
01:41:18,256 --> 01:41:20,087
The Terminator knew.

727
01:41:20,592 --> 01:41:23,083
He tried to tell us...

728
01:41:23,929 --> 01:41:26,625
...but I didn't want to hear it.

729
01:41:28,934 --> 01:41:32,927
Maybe the future has been written. I don't know.

730
01:41:33,939 --> 01:41:36,601
All I know is what the Terminator taught me:

731
01:41:37,275 --> 01:41:39,607
Never stop fighting.

732
01:41:39,778 --> 01:41:42,440
And I never will .

733
01:41:44,449 --> 01:41:48,408
The battle has just begun.

734
01:41:48,408 --> 01:41:51,408
谢谢观赏

